# No em dashes in product copy

Never use the em dash character (`—`) or en dash (`–`) in **user-facing** text: landing, FAQ, UI strings, toasts, emails, `llms.txt`, JSON-LD, marketing.

Use a period, comma, colon, or parentheses instead.

Examples:
- Bad: `1er scan sans compte — gratuit`
- Good: `1er scan sans compte. Gratuit`
- Bad: `Yes — your bar is at 50%`
- Good: `Yes: your bar is at 50%`

Code comments may keep dashes if needed; product copy must not.
